From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 05:10:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: G16: dep_stats counts and hold times for
 kernel-resolved dependencies

To measure what kernel-side ordering costs per frame, count per queue:
- renders whose tiling stage was ordered after an earlier fragment stamp in
  the kernel;
- admissions deferred on that stamp, and on compute or other-queue stamps;
- fragment-stage waits dropped as already ordered by the lane;
- compute admissions deferred on other queues.
With dep_stats=1 the counts are logged once when the queue is destroyed:
"G16: queue deps renders= computes= ta_ordered= ta_held= cross_held=
lane_dropped= compute_held=".

Folded in:
- drm/asahi: G16 dep_stats: per-queue counts of kernel-resolved dependencies
- drm/asahi: G16 dep_stats: report how long kernel-resolved dependencies hold Works

[drm/asahi: G16 dep_stats: report how long kernel-resolved dependencies hold Works]
Add the number of Works admitted after at least one deferral and their
total time from first deferral to admission, so the throughput cost of
kernel-side ordering can be read per queue after a run.

Signed-off-by: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit d67bf5d0e0cd246022c032f3a9a384803aa8d4a6)
